+	/*
+	 * IMAGE 282 -- the UCHE's GMEM (on-chip memory) window.
+	 *
+	 * We program [0x100000 : 0x100000 + gpu->gmem - 1], and gpu->gmem is
+	 * ZERO for a6xx in this tree (the per-chip info has no .gmem), so the
+	 * window we program is the degenerate 0x100000..0x0FFFFF.
+	 *
+	 * CAF programs it with its own formula
+	 * (drivers/gpu/msm/adreno.c:848-851, adreno_a6xx.c:822-828):
+	 *
+	 *   uche_gmem_base = ALIGN(gmem_size, SZ_1M);
+	 *   GMEM_RANGE_MIN = uche_gmem_base;
+	 *   GMEM_RANGE_MAX = uche_gmem_base + gmem_size - 1;
+	 *
+	 * with gmem_size = 256K -> [0x100000, 0x13FFFF].
+	 *
+	 * If the shader's private memory is misrouted out of the GMEM window
+	 * it would land in the system-memory path -- the path that is broken
+	 * for the 3D domain while the CP's works -- and a shader that cannot
+	 * use its scratch memory would never reach its stores.
