+ *     Verified live: /sys/bus/platform/devices/2ca0000.kgsl-smmu -> arm-smmu
+ *
+ *   - The context banks are declared as children carrying standard "iommus"
+ *     properties, so the generic IOMMU API can consume them directly:
+ *         gfx3d_user     iommus = <&qsmmu 0x0 0x401>   CB 0, SID 0x401
+ *         gfx3d_secure   iommus = <&qsmmu 0x2 0x400>   CB 2, SID 0x400
+ *         gmu_user       iommus = <&qsmmu 0x4 0x400>   CB 4, SID 0x400
+ *         gmu_kernel     iommus = <&qsmmu 0x5 0x400>   CB 5, SID 0x400
+ *
+ *   - CAF itself obtains these CBs with nothing but of_platform_populate(),
+ *     of_find_device_by_node(), of_dma_configure(), iommu_domain_alloc() and
+ *     iommu_attach_device(). See drivers/gpu/msm/kgsl_iommu.c:_kgsl_iommu_probe()
+ *     and drivers/gpu/msm/kgsl_gmu.c:gmu_iommu_cb_probe().
+ *
+ * So this file re-implements exactly that sequence and nothing more. It
+ * deliberately does NOT reimplement SMMU register programming, does NOT touch
+ * the SDE/display MMU path, and does NOT re-enable KGSL.
+ *
+ * CONTEXT-BANK ASSIGNMENT (traced from the KGSL reference, not guessed)
+ * =====================================================================
+ *
+ *   GPU core (a6xx)     -> gfx3d_user    (CB 0, SID 0x401)
+ *   GMU kernel buffers  -> gmu_kernel    (CB 5, SID 0x400)
+ *       HFI queues, A640 icache/dcache, debug region. Confirmed against
+ *       kgsl_gmu.c, which maps GMU kernel memory with GMU_CONTEXT_KERNEL.
+ *   GMU user pages      -> gmu_user      (CB 4)  - process pages only
+ *   GPU secure buffers  -> gfx3d_secure  (CB 2)  - secure allocs only
+ *
+ * The last two are not needed to bring the GPU up and are not requested here.
